    {
      "name": "sess_request",
      "description": "Use it when you need the person's approval, a decision or details only they can give before you go on, even if they only say 'ask me' or 'check with me' and name no tool or device. Not for clarifying what they just asked, or for anything you can work out yourself. It is the full form, with approve and reject buttons if you need them; sess_ask is shorter for a plain question. Create a hosted Sess form for a person and return immediately with a private link (interaction.humanUrl) and a handle. Give the link only to the intended person in this private conversation; anyone holding it can answer. A receipt records what was shown and chosen, not who answered. Then call sess_response with the handle and revision. Do not call sess_request again for the same question. Keep it short: a title of about 40 characters (at most 80), button labels a verb of 1-3 words (at most 24), field labels at most 60, help one hint (at most 160). A value over its limit is refused with INVALID_ARGUMENTS naming the field (a JSON pointer), the limit, its length and the fix; nothing is truncated. Shorten that value and call again.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "interaction": {
            "type": "object",
            "description": "A Sess form: a title, components shown in order and 1-5 buttons. Keep it short: a person reads it on a phone. A value over its limit is refused with INVALID_ARGUMENTS naming the field (a JSON pointer), the limit, its length and the fix; nothing is truncated. Shorten that value and call again.",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "required": [
              "mode",
              "title",
              "source",
              "actions"
            ],
            "examples": [
              {
                "mode": "interactive",
                "title": "Approve this commit?",
                "description": "Check the message before I commit.",
                "source": {
                  "kind": "sess_surface",
